{
  "id": "ASTIS-RT-20261005-SPHMCImplementedPhaseQueryWork",
  "state": "source-reviewed",
  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:sphmc-implemented-phase-query-work",
    "anchor": "Algorithm 3.1 and Lemma D.4, actual query centers before Jensen; D.7 and D.8 remain separate",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#A4.SS2",
    "original_text": "E is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel sigma-algebra; i ranges over a finite index type of size J.\nV is C2, kappa>=1, and kappa^(-1)||v||^2 <= D2V(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2 for all x,v. Its actual gradient vanishes at the supplied xstar.\n0<eta<=c<1, eps>0, h>=0, M>=0, S>=0. The incoming probability law nu on (X,P) has integrable ||X-xstar||^2+||P||^2, with integral at most M.\nThe supplied deterministic nodes satisfy |t_i|<=1 and each supplied omega row satisfies sum_j |omega_ij|<=S. Position and momentum weights are arbitrary supplied real arrays; source Chebyshev quadrature is not instantiated.\nFor the full independent driving law gamma=(Gaussian zeta0 product Gaussian zeta1) product (Gaussian array G0 product Gaussian array G1), and mu=nu product gamma, set a=exp(-h/2), sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)), MR=M+(1-exp(-h))*d, B=6MR+3eps^2+3eta*d and C=2+(1+log((1-c)^(-1)))/(-log c), d=finrank(E). There exist the same measurable exact proximal map p, actual stopped output q and natural index N, with p(y)+eta grad V(p(y))=y, ||q(y)-p(y)||<=eps and run(grad V,eta,eps,y,N(y)+1,y)=some(q(y),N(y)+1) for every y. Define P0=aP+sigma zeta0, Y0_i=X+t_i P0, Z0_j=grad V(q(Y0_j)+sqrt(eta) G0_j), Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j, Z1_j=grad V(q(Y1_j)+sqrt(eta) G1_j), and Phi=(X+h P0-sum_j positionWeight_j Z1_j, a(P0-sum_j momentumWeight_j Z1_j)+sigma zeta1). Phi is measurable and gives a Markov kernel K(s)=gamma.map(z -> Phi(s,z)). For every i both gradient squares are integrable, with E_mu||grad V(Y0_i)||^2<=2MR and E_mu||grad V(Y1_i)||^2<=4MR+2S^2 B. Both actual counts N(Y0_i)+1 and N(Y1_i)+1 are integrable; their respective expectations are at most C[1+log(1+sqrt(2MR)/eps)] and C[1+log(1+sqrt(4MR+2S^2 B)/eps)].",
    "text_sha256": "29d82e039d1110f38dffbe5fd3e085fe0f38098d6ca2ea88d868729eedd81c51"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.ImplementedPhaseWork.implemented_phase_query_moments_and_work",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/ImplementedPhaseWork.lean",
    "statement": "{E ι : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [Fintype ι]\n{V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ≥0}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (κ : ℝ)⁻¹ * ‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ ‖v‖^2)\n    {eta c eps : ℝ} (heta : 0 < eta) (hec : eta ≤ c) (hc : c < 1) (heps : 0 < eps)\n    (ν : Measure (E × E)) [IsProbabilityMeasure ν]\n    (xstar : E) (hstar : gradient V xstar = 0)\n    {h M S : ℝ} (hh : 0 ≤ h) (hM : 0 ≤ M) (hS : 0 ≤ S)\n    (hstateI : Integrable (fun s : E × E => ‖s.1-xstar‖^2 + ‖s.2‖^2) ν)\n    (hstate : (∫ s : E × E, ‖s.1-xstar‖^2 + ‖s.2‖^2 ∂ν) ≤ M)\n    (t : ι → ℝ) (ht : ∀ i, |t i| ≤ 1) (omega : ι → ι → ℝ)\n    (hrow : ∀ i, (∑ j, |omega i j|) ≤ S)\n    (positionWeight momentumWeight : ι → ℝ) :\n    let a := Real.exp (-h/2)\n    let sigma := Real.sqrt (1-Real.exp (-h))\n    let gi := Measure.pi (fun _ : ι => stdGaussian E)\n    let γ := ((stdGaussian E).prod (stdGaussian E)).prod (gi.prod gi)\n    let μ := ν.prod γ\n    let MR := M + (1-Real.exp (-h)) * (Module.finrank ℝ E : ℝ)\n    let B := 6*MR + 3*eps^2 + 3*eta*(Module.finrank ℝ E : ℝ)\n    let C := 2 + (1+Real.log ((1-c)⁻¹))/(-Real.log c)\n    ∃ p q : E → E, ∃ N : E → ℕ,\n      Measurable p ∧ Measurable q ∧ Measurable N ∧\n      (∀ y, p y + eta • gradient V (p y) = y ∧ ‖q y-p y‖ ≤ eps ∧\n        run (gradient V) eta eps y (N y+1) y =\n          some (q y,N y+1)) ∧\n      let P0 := fun w : (E × E) × ((E × E) × ((ι → E) × (ι → E))) =>\n        a • w.1.2 + sigma • w.2.1.1\n      let Y0 := fun i w => w.1.1 + t i • P0 w\n      let Z0 := fun j w => gradient V (q (Y0 j w) + Real.sqrt eta • w.2.2.1 j)\n      let Y1 := fun i w => Y0 i w - ∑ j, omega i j • Z0 j w\n      let Z1 := fun j w => gradient V (q (Y1 j w) + Real.sqrt eta • w.2.2.2 j)\n      let Φ := fun w => (w.1.1 + h • P0 w - ∑ j, positionWeight j • Z1 j w,\n        a • (P0 w - ∑ j, momentumWeight j • Z1 j w) + sigma • w.2.1.2)\n      Measurable Φ ∧ ∃ K : Kernel (E × E) (E × E), IsMarkovKernel K ∧\n      (∀ s, K s = γ.map (fun z => Φ (s,z))) ∧\n      (∀ i, Integrable (fun w => ‖gradient V (Y0 i w)‖^2) μ ∧\n        (∫ w, ‖gradient V (Y0 i w)‖^2 ∂μ) ≤ 2*MR ∧\n        Integrable (fun w => (N (Y0 i w) : ℝ)+1) μ ∧\n        (∫ w, (N (Y0 i w) : ℝ)+1 ∂μ) ≤\n          C*(1+Real.log (1+Real.sqrt (2*MR)/eps))) ∧\n      (∀ i, Integrable (fun w => ‖gradient V (Y1 i w)‖^2) μ ∧\n        (∫ w, ‖gradient V (Y1 i w)‖^2 ∂μ) ≤ 4*MR+2*S^2*B ∧\n        Integrable (fun w => (N (Y1 i w) : ℝ)+1) μ ∧\n        (∫ w, (N (Y1 i w) : ℝ)+1 ∂μ) ≤\n          C*(1+Real.log (1+Real.sqrt (4*MR+2*S^2*B)/eps)))",
    "statement_sha256": "3a89ed37db282e55cc8c54ca12e6350fb3700df173935d73f7db7cf3ec361cfe",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability law. Measure.pi over a finite index type is the independent Gaussian array law; Measure.prod is independent product; Measure.map is measurable pushforward. Kernel is a measurable probability-kernel API; IsMarkovKernel means each output law is a probability measure.",
      "Integrable is Bochner integrability for the specified measure. gradient is the real inner-product gradient; fderiv is the Frechet derivative; finrank is real dimension. Finite sums use all elements of the finite index type.",
      "The finite interpreter run(g,eta,eps,y,fuel,x) returns none at zero fuel. With positive fuel it evaluates g(x), sets next=y-eta*g(x), returns some(x,1) if ||next-x||<=(1-eta)*eps, otherwise recurses from next with one less fuel and adds one to a successful returned query count. Arithmetic is exact real arithmetic. Natural counts cast to the reals include the final successful gradient test."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Focused Lean compiled with repository-pinned Lean4.33.0 and Mathlib db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d. Test prints standard propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound only."
  },
