    "review_run_sha256": "368637d201d33d59e8e5e11d580e345682b24555947f1c35f2893d71a1614035",
    "evidence": "This independent anti-anchored review started from ImplementedPhaseWork.source-review.json, not a draft audit, previous verdict or previous review output. No prior review classification was used. Canonical packet sha256 0ee6e71a2956228fd5916e7fcb0238534ee85a5fc7455814e06ec407590a69aa and raw packet sha256 d76b289765e47d1dcc080560973ba435710f897cfc70d4c31ab965af04f9bcbd were recomputed; source text, exact Lean statement and blind-reconstruction text hashes all match. Checked base HEAD 6410634a18e787d1e8d09e02a75a28c623398967 and the complete current module text supplied in candidate_publication_context. Normalized publication module digest e7a78dcc021dc489bfd56728286ca2c8705a54b29d6aa3c2717da5db0580f94a matches the live complete text; raw module bytes sha256 e7a78dcc021dc489bfd56728286ca2c8705a54b29d6aa3c2717da5db0580f94a. Current publication binding e40842e0549d6a7783d6e499c7f104c1dacbba050f8aa9d2f7f5b3173bbea2b3. Live primary source https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1 was inspected at Algorithm D.2/D.3 and D.4 lines 2138-2186, and Algorithm 3.1 formulas were checked for the phase component. The entire ImplementedPhaseWork module, including private first_input_projection_preserving, was independently checked. Both first-coordinate product projections preserve probability measures; their product with the identity on nu followed by inverse association gives exactly the helper stated map and marginal. No factor or coordinate is swapped. The complete PicardInputLaw, PartialMomentumRefresh and PicardCenterMoment proofs were read. The refresh proof uses independent zero-mean Gaussian noise to cancel the cross term and adds sigma^2*d; its incoming P/X law may be internally correlated. The input-law proof adjoins G0 and proves each Gaussian coordinate square moment d. These facts pull back along the exact full-law projection. The center parent uses normalized gradient Lipschitzness, proximal nonexpansiveness and p(xstar)=xstar; pointwise domination proves first-center square moment <=2MR and first stochastic-gradient square moment <=B. Weighted Cauchy-Schwarz yields the row square moment <=S^2B, hence second-center/gradient square moment <=4MR+2S^2B. Integrability is separately established by the same measurable integrable envelopes. The full phase and moment witnesses are matched by successful pair uniqueness; both q and N, not just a count, agree. The previously read current realized-work/Jensen module then gives the actual N(Y)+1 expectation and integrability for each layer. Nonnegative C and eps positivity justify moment-bound substitution under sqrt/log. The kernel retains independent G1 and the final refresh even though second-center moments require only the first-noise marginal. Source coefficients and repeated-history/total-cost bounds are not silently imported. The six-step authored formula proof accurately covers the private helper, corrected MR, witness identification, both layer moments, both costs and full output law. Fresh LEAN_NUM_THREADS=2 lake env lean Tests/SmoothedPicardHMCImplementedPhaseWork.lean exited 0. It printed only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound for both exact declarations. The test instantiates a positive-time one-dimensional two-node actual phase from a zero-state Dirac incoming law and derives, rather than assumes, actual center-square integrability and both count integrabilities. The only warning was an unused binder. Focused fake-closure scan of ImplementedPhaseWork, ProximalExecutionIdentity, PicardInputLaw, PicardCenterMoment and PartialMomentumRefresh found no sorry, admit, axiom, Prop:=True or :=trivial. The entire current authored statement, all assumptions, formula proof steps and actual ASTIS dependency list were inspected. No remaining blocking mathematical/source/exposition gap is found within this pinned component. This verdict does not complete D.7, D.8, quadrature instantiation or a main theorem.",
