          "title": "Marginalize the full innovation law exactly",
          "text": "Project ((state,(zeta0,zeta1)),(G0,G1)) to ((state,zeta0),G0). Probability-product first-coordinate projections preserve measure. Their product, followed by inverse product association, gives exactly the input law (nu product Gaussian) product Gaussian-array. Thus omitted zeta1 and G1 factors integrate to one; independence is present in the law, not inferred from TV closeness.",
          "formula": "\\operatorname{proj}_\\#(\\nu\\otimes[(\\gamma_E\\otimes\\gamma_E)\\otimes(\\gamma_E^\\iota\\otimes\\gamma_E^\\iota)])=(\\nu\\otimes\\gamma_E)\\otimes\\gamma_E^\\iota.",
          "lean": "first_input_projection_preserving; measurePreserving_fst; MeasurePreserving.prod; measurePreserving_prodAssoc"
        },
