          "title": "Derive the corrected refresh and Gaussian budgets",
          "text": "Apply the compiled input-law theorem to the incoming state law and the first half-refresh. Pull its L2 integrability and bound, and the exact Gaussian coordinate second moments, back along the measure-preserving projection. The refreshed budget is MR, including the positive innovation contribution (1-exp(-h))*d. The proof does not silently reuse M after adding noise.",
          "formula": "\\mathbb E_\\mu[\\|X-x_*\\|^2+\\|P_0\\|^2]\\le M_R,\\qquad \\mathbb E_\\mu\\|G_j^0\\|^2=d.",
